      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“Interdependence” by Dorothy Canfield Fisher (1879-1958) was originally written for the 50th Anniversary of the World’s Young Women’s Christian Association, 19 November 1944. The prayer was included by Rabbi Morrison David Bial in his anthology, <tei:hi rend="italic">An Offering of Prayer</tei:hi> (1962), p. 55. It’s likely that Rabbi Bial first read the prayer in an anthology of prayer by Stephen Hole Fritchman, <tei:hi rend="italic">Prayers of the Free Spirit</tei:hi> (1945), p. 38.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
